        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "316b28fa-32cf-5d68-84d0-16485785287e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Bob McDill, Mel McDaniel, Don Williams, Wayne Pride\n- Songs: \"Louisiana Saturday Night\"\n- Albums: \"I'm Countryfied\"\n- Roles: country singer, songwriter, opening act\n- Organizations: Country Music Hall of Fame\n\nFacts:\n- Don Williams was born Donald Ray Williams on May 27, 1939, and he was an American country singer and songwriter.\n- \"Louisiana Saturday Night\" was written by Bob McDill and was originally sung by Don Williams.\n- Mel McDaniel recorded \"Louisiana Saturday Night.\"\n- Mel McDaniel released \"Louisiana Saturday Night\" in March 1981 as the third single from his 1980 album \"I'm Countryfied.\"\n- Wayne Pride was the opening act for Don Williams in early 2004.\n- Don Williams was inducted into the Country Music Hall of Fame in 2010.\n- Don Williams was known as the \"Gentle Giant\" of country music because of his straightforward smooth bass-baritone voice, soft tones, and imposing build.\n- Don Williams died on September 8, 2017.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "4dd6377f-9931-5969-aee0-2fda05c1e9a2",
        "text": "Page: Louisiana Saturday Night. Sentence: \"Louisiana Saturday Night\" is a song written by Bob McDill and recorded by American country music artist, Mel McDaniel.\nPage: Louisiana Saturday Night. Sentence: It was released in March 1981 as the third single from McDaniel's 1980 album, \"I'm Countryfied\".\nPage: Louisiana Saturday Night. Sentence: The song was originally sung by Don Williams.\nPage: Don Williams. Sentence: Don Williams (born Donald Ray Williams; May 27, 1939 – September 8, 2017) was an American country singer, songwriter, and 2010 inductee to the Country Music Hall of Fame.\nPage: Don Williams. Sentence: His straightforward yet smooth bass-baritone voice, soft tones, and imposing build earned him the nickname: \"Gentle Giant\" of country music.\nPage: Wayne Pride. Sentence: He was the opening act for Don Williams in early 2004.",
